## Lessons Learned

The primary lesson from this issue was the importance of troubleshooting infrastructure problems systematically rather than assuming the first visible symptom represents the root cause.

DNS, networking, and Active Directory are closely interconnected. A problem appearing to be an Active Directory issue may originate from network or DNS configuration.
